# KISS

Keep it simple. Write the smallest design that meets the requirement. Add a branch, helper, or abstraction only when the straight-line version is unclear.

- One function, one job, early returns.
- A few duplicated lines beat a helper with one caller.
- Use what the repo already depends on. No new library for a one-off.
- Flatten or split when a limit below fires. Do not disable this rule to land a change.

## Limits

- Cyclomatic complexity ≤ 10
- Cognitive complexity ≤ 15
- Block nesting ≤ 3
- Nested callbacks ≤ 3
- Parameters ≤ 4
- Function length ≤ 80 lines, ignoring blanks and comments. Specs and e2e tests skip the line cap only.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — flags and nesting for a single read
function load(id: string, opts: { retry?: boolean; cache?: boolean }) {
  if (opts.retry) {
    if (opts.cache) return readCached(id);
  }
  return read(id);
}

// ✅ GOOD
async function loadRepository(id: string) {
  const snapshot = await collection().doc(id).get();
  if (!snapshot.exists) return null;
  return { id: snapshot.id, ...snapshot.data() };
}
```
